<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Sounds Impossible, But It's Not — Tiffani Swensen | Simply Home</title>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;500;600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  html { scroll-behavior: smooth; scroll-snap-type: y mandatory; }
  body {
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
    background: #0a0a0a;
    color: #e2e8f0;
    line-height: 1.7;
    overflow-x: hidden;
  }
  .container { max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px; }
  .animate-on-scroll {
    opacity: 0; transform: translateY(24px);
    transition: all 0.7s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
  }
  .animate-on-scroll.visible { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
  @keyframes shimmer {
    0%, 100% { background-position: 0% 50%; }
    50% { background-position: 100% 50%; }
  }
  section {
    min-height: 100vh;
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    padding: 48px 24px;
    scroll-snap-align: start; scroll-snap-stop: always;
    position: relative;
  }
  section .container { width: 100%; }

  /* HERO */
  .hero {
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, #0f172a 0%, #0a0a0a 100%);
    position: relative;
  }
  .hero::before {
    content: ''; position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; height: 60%;
    background: radial-gradient(ellipse at 50% 0%, rgba(20, 184, 166, 0.1) 0%, transparent 60%);
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .hero-content { text-align: center; position: relative; z-index: 1; }
  .hero-logo { width: 160px; margin-bottom: 28px; opacity: 0.9; }
  .hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 4.2rem); font-weight: 800;
    margin-bottom: 14px; letter-spacing: -0.03em; line-height: 0.95;
    color: #f8fafc;
  }
  .hero h1 span {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #14b8a6 0%, #5eead4 50%, #14b8a6 100%);
    background-size: 200% auto;
    -webkit-background-clip: text; -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
    background-clip: text; animation: shimmer 3s ease infinite;
  }
  .hero-subtitle {
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.8vw, 1.2rem); color: #64748b;
    max-width: 480px; margin: 0 auto; line-height: 1.5; font-weight: 400;
  }

  /* HEADERS */
  .slide-header { text-align: center; margin-bottom: 32px; }
  .slide-num {
    font-size: 0.7rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px;
    color: #475569; margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .slide-title {
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.2rem); font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 6px; letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: #f8fafc;
  }
  .slide-tag { color: #64748b; font-size: 0.9rem; }

  /* CARDS */
  .card {
    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.02);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05);
    border-radius: 18px;
    padding: 28px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .story {
    font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.85; color: #cbd5e1;
  }
  .story p { margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .story p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .story strong { color: #f8fafc; font-weight: 500; }

  .teal { color: #14b8a6; font-weight: 500; }
  .amber { color: #fbbf24; font-weight: 500; }
  .rose { color: #f87171; font-weight: 500; }

  /* ISSUE / ANSWER BOXES */
  .box {
    border-radius: 14px;
    padding: 18px 22px;
    margin-top: 14px;
  }
  .issue-box { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.015); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05); }
  .answer-box { background: rgba(20, 184, 166, 0.04); border: 1px solid rgba(20, 184, 166, 0.1); }
  .insight-box { background: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.1); }
  .stat-box { background: rgba(30, 41, 59, 0.4); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.04); }

  .box-label {
    font-size: 0.65rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px;
    margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: 600;
  }
  .issue-box .box-label { color: #475569; }
  .answer-box .box-label { color: #14b8a6; }
  .insight-box .box-label { color: #fbbf24; }
  .stat-box .box-label { color: #64748b; }

  .box-item {
    padding: 7px 0;
    font-size: 0.93rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.035);
  }
  .box-item:last-child { border-bottom: none; padding-bottom: 0; }
  .box-item:first-child { padding-top: 0; }

  .divider {
    width: 28px; height: 2px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, #14b8a6, transparent);
    border-radius: 1px; margin: 14px 0;
  }

  .insight-quote {
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #cbd5e1;
  }
  .insight-quote em { color: #fbbf24; font-style: normal; font-weight: 500; }

  /* COMPARISON */
  .compare { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 12px; margin-top: 14px; }
  .compare-col {
    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.02);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05);
    border-radius: 14px;
    padding: 18px;
  }
  .compare-col .box-label { color: #475569; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .compare-col ul { list-style: none; }
  .compare-col li { color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.9rem; padding: 3px 0; }

  /* CONTACT */
  .contact-box {
    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.02);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05);
    border-radius: 20px; padding: 36px 28px; text-align: center;
  }
  .qr { width: 150px; height: 150px; border-radius: 14px; margin-bottom: 22px; opacity: 0.9; }
  .btn {
    padding: 12px 26px; border-radius: 50px; font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none; transition: all 0.3s ease;
    font-size: 0.9rem; display: inline-block; margin: 3px;
  }
  .btn-primary {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #14b8a6 0%, #0d9488 100%);
    color: #0a0a0a;
  }
  .btn-primary:hover { transform: translateY(-2px); }
  .btn-secondary {
    background: transparent; color: #94a3b8;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
  }
  .btn-secondary:hover { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.04); }

  footer {
    background: #0a0a0a; padding: 32px 24px; text-align: center;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.03);
  }
  footer p { color: #334155; font-size: 0.75rem; }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .compare { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<!-- === SLIDE 1: HERO === -->
<section class="hero">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="hero-content">
      <img src="simply-home-logo-wide.webp" alt="Simply Home" class="hero-logo">
      <h1><span>Sounds Impossible,</span><br>But It's Not</h1>
      <p class="hero-subtitle">Three clients. Three obstacles. And the strategy that changed everything.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- === SLIDE 2: HOOK === -->
<section style="background: linear-gradient(180deg, #0f172a 0%, #0a0a0a 100%);">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="slide-header">
      <div class="slide-num"></div>
      <h2 class="slide-title">Before We Begin</h2>
      <p class="slide-tag"></p>
    </div>
    <div class="card animate-on-scroll" style="text-align:center; padding: 36px 28px;">
      <div class="story" style="font-size: 1.15rem;">
        <p>Quick show of hands,<br><strong>has a lender ever told you or someone you know <span class="rose">"no"</span>?</strong></p>
        <p style="margin-top: 20px; color: #64748b; font-size: 1rem;">Today: three people who heard no.<br>Here's what made it yes.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- === SLIDE 3: S1 PROBLEM === -->
<section style="background: #0a0a0a;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="slide-header">
      <div class="slide-num">Scenario 1 of 3</div>
      <h2 class="slide-title">The Job-Hopping Veteran</h2>
      <p class="slide-tag">Jake's story, why lenders said no</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card animate-on-scroll">
      <div class="story">
        <p>"Hi, I'm Jake. I'm a veteran who served our country, and I have my Certificate of Eligibility, which means I can buy a home with <span class="teal">zero money down</span>. I've been wanting to buy for a while.</p>
        <p>But here's the thing, over the past two years, I've had <span class="amber">six different jobs</span>. They've all been in the same field, but I know how that looks on paper. I'm also <strong>100% disabled</strong>, which adds another layer of concern. Every lender I've talked to has made it clear: I'm not their ideal borrower."</p>
      </div>
      <div class="box issue-box">
        <div class="box-label">Why Traditional Lenders Said No</div>
        <div class="box-item">❌ <span class="rose">Six job changes in two years</span>, seen as unstable</div>
        <div class="box-item">❌ <span class="rose">100% disabled</span>, perceived as complicated</div>
        <div class="box-item">❌ Assumed unqualified despite having a COE</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- === SLIDE 4: S1 SOLUTION === -->
<section style="background: linear-gradient(180deg, #0a0a0a 0%, #0f172a 100%);">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="slide-header">
      <div class="slide-num">The Solution</div>
      <h2 class="slide-title">The Job-Hopping Veteran</h2>
      <p class="slide-tag">Jake, how each barrier was removed</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card animate-on-scroll">
      <div class="box answer-box">
        <div class="box-label">Barrier 1: Six Jobs in Two Years</div>
        <div class="box-item">✅ Every job was in the <strong>same industry</strong></div>
        <div class="box-item">✅ Never more than a <span class="teal">3-day gap</span> between positions, that is consistency, not chaos</div>
        <div class="box-item">✅ Qualified for a <strong>VA loan</strong> with his COE</div>
      </div>
      <div class="box answer-box">
        <div class="box-label">Barrier 2: Disability Status</div>
        <div class="box-item">✅ <span class="amber">Property taxes removed entirely</span>, a benefit for 100% disabled veterans</div>
        <div class="box-item">✅ Lower monthly payment, more monthly savings</div>
      </div>
      <div class="box insight-box" style="margin-top: 16px;">
        <div class="box-label">What I Saw That Others Missed</div>
        <div class="insight-quote">"Other lenders saw six jobs. I saw <em>six proofs he could get hired</em> in his field."</div>
      </div>
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <div class="story">
        <p><strong>Jake bought his home.</strong> What looked like a liability on the surface told a completely different story once someone took the time to understand it.</p>
        <p style="margin-top: 12px; color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.95rem;"><span class="amber">$200+/month</span> back in his pocket from property tax removal alone. That means something.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- === SLIDE 5: S2 PROBLEM === -->
<section style="background: #0a0a0a;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="slide-header">
      <div class="slide-num">Scenario 2 of 3</div>
      <h2 class="slide-title">The Contingent Buyer</h2>
      <p class="slide-tag">Emily's story, caught between two homes</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card animate-on-scroll">
      <div class="story">
        <p>"Hi, I'm Emily. I own a home in Herriman, but I've been wanting to move to <strong>Cottonwood Heights</strong> for a while, it's closer to work, better schools for my kids, just a better fit for where my family is right now.</p>
        <p>The challenge is the market there. It's competitive. I was told that if my offer depends on selling my current home first, sellers won't even consider it. I understand where they're coming from, but that leaves me in a tough spot, I need to sell to buy, but I can't buy without selling first."</p>
      </div>
      <div class="box issue-box">
        <div class="box-label">Why Traditional Lenders Said No</div>
        <div class="box-item">❌ <span class="rose">Contingent offers</span> rejected in competitive markets</div>
        <div class="box-item">❌ Conventional DTI too tight, can't qualify for two mortgages</div>
        <div class="box-item">❌ Seemed forced to sell first, rent, then buy</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- === SLIDE 6: S2 SOLUTION === -->
<section style="background: linear-gradient(180deg, #0a0a0a 0%, #0f172a 100%);">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="slide-header">
      <div class="slide-num">The Solution</div>
      <h2 class="slide-title">The Contingent Buyer</h2>
      <p class="slide-tag">Emily, how each barrier was removed</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card animate-on-scroll">
      <div class="box answer-box">
        <div class="box-label">Barrier 1: Can't Get Offer Accepted</div>
        <div class="box-item">✅ Evaluated options beyond conventional loans</div>
        <div class="box-item">✅ <span class="teal">FHA</span> has more flexible DTI guidelines</div>
        <div class="box-item">✅ Emily qualified to carry <strong>both mortgages</strong></div>
        <div class="box-item">✅ Made an offer <span class="amber">without a contingency</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="box answer-box">
        <div class="box-label">Barrier 2: Sell First, Then Buy</div>
        <div class="box-item">✅ Closed on the new house first</div>
        <div class="box-item">✅ Had <strong>two weeks</strong> to move at her own pace</div>
        <div class="box-item">✅ Sold the Herriman home after moving out</div>
        <div class="box-item">✅ <span class="amber">No bridge loan. No double move.</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="box insight-box" style="margin-top: 16px;">
        <div class="box-label">What I Saw That Others Missed</div>
        <div class="insight-quote">"Other lenders saw a buyer who needed to sell. I saw <em>a buyer who could carry two mortgages</em>."</div>
      </div>
      <div class="compare" style="margin-top: 16px;">
        <div class="compare-col">
          <div class="box-label">Without This Strategy</div>
          <ul>
            <li>Sell current home</li>
            <li>Find a rental</li>
            <li>Move once</li>
            <li>Buy new home</li>
            <li>Move again</li>
            <li>2+ months of chaos</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="compare-col">
          <div class="box-label">With FHA Strategy</div>
          <ul>
            <li>Buy new home</li>
            <li>Move once</li>
            <li>Sell from new home</li>
            <li>No bridge loan needed</li>
            <li>No double move</li>
            <li>Seamless transition</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <div class="story">
        <p><strong>Emily got her Cottonwood Heights home.</strong> The solution wasn't waiting for the market to change, it was finding a loan program that fit her actual situation.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- === SLIDE 7: S3 PROBLEM === -->
<section style="background: #0a0a0a;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="slide-header">
      <div class="slide-num">Scenario 3 of 3</div>
      <h2 class="slide-title">The Cash-Strapped Investor</h2>
      <p class="slide-tag">Tom's story, great deal, wrong paperwork</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card animate-on-scroll">
      <div class="story">
        <p>"Hi, I'm Tom. I'm self-employed, and I've been investing in real estate for a while. I found a <span class="amber">$400,000 property</span> that's fairly priced with huge upside, it's exactly the kind of deal I look for. I need <strong>25% down</strong>, about $100,000.</p>
        <p>The issue is cash flow. I'm self-employed, my income is solid, but it doesn't look like a W-2, so traditional lenders aren't sure how to evaluate me. I own another investment property free and clear, so I know I have equity, but I haven't been able to access it in a way that works for this deal. Without $100K liquid, I'm stuck."</p>
      </div>
      <div class="box issue-box">
        <div class="box-label">Why Traditional Lenders Said No</div>
        <div class="box-item">❌ Needs <span class="rose">$100K down</span>, no liquid cash available</div>
        <div class="box-item">❌ <span class="rose">Self-employed</span>, income doesn't fit traditional verification</div>
        <div class="box-item">❌ Has equity in another property but can't access it conventionally</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- === SLIDE 8: S3 SOLUTION === -->
<section style="background: linear-gradient(180deg, #0a0a0a 0%, #0f172a 100%);">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="slide-header">
      <div class="slide-num">The Solution</div>
      <h2 class="slide-title">The Cash-Strapped Investor</h2>
      <p class="slide-tag">Tom, how each barrier was removed</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card animate-on-scroll">
      <div class="box answer-box">
        <div class="box-label">Barrier 1: No Cash for Down Payment</div>
        <div class="box-item">✅ Structured <span class="teal">cash-out DSCR loan</span> on paid-off property</div>
        <div class="box-item">✅ Pulled <strong>$100K</strong> from existing equity</div>
        <div class="box-item">✅ Used as down payment on new property</div>
      </div>
      <div class="box answer-box">
        <div class="box-label">Barrier 2: Self-Employed Income</div>
        <div class="box-item">✅ DSCR loan uses <strong>property income</strong>, not personal income</div>
        <div class="box-item">✅ Self-employed status = <span class="amber">completely irrelevant</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="box answer-box">
        <div class="box-label">Barrier 3: Will the Property Cash Flow?</div>
        <div class="box-item">✅ Two separate entrances = <strong>two rental units</strong></div>
        <div class="box-item">✅ ~$2,500 total rent covers the new mortgage</div>
        <div class="box-item">✅ Property pays for itself</div>
      </div>
      <div class="box insight-box" style="margin-top: 16px;">
        <div class="box-label">What I Saw That Others Missed</div>
        <div class="insight-quote">"Other lenders saw self-employed. I saw <em>a property that would pay for itself</em>."</div>
      </div>
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <div class="story">
        <p><strong>Tom closed the deal.</strong> Zero personal income used. Zero cash out of pocket. One smart loan structure.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- === SLIDE 9: STATS / THESE AREN'T OUTLIERS === -->
<section style="background: #0a0a0a;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="slide-header">
      <div class="slide-num">The Pattern</div>
      <h2 class="slide-title">These Aren't Outliers</h2>
      <p class="slide-tag">The programs that make these deals work</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card animate-on-scroll">
      <div class="box stat-box" style="margin-top: 0;">
        <div class="box-label">VA Loans</div>
        <div class="box-item" style="color: #cbd5e1; border: none; padding: 4px 0;"><span class="teal">528,000+</span> veterans bought homes with VA loans in FY2025, up 27% year over year. The program just guaranteed its <strong>29 millionth</strong> loan since 1944.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="box stat-box" style="margin-top: 12px;">
        <div class="box-label">FHA Loans</div>
        <div class="box-item" style="color: #cbd5e1; border: none; padding: 4px 0;">In 2025, FHA helped <span class="teal">236,000+</span> buyers, including <span class="teal">140,000+</span> first-timers. When conventional says no, FHA often says yes.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="box stat-box" style="margin-top: 12px;">
        <div class="box-label">DSCR Loans</div>
        <div class="box-item" style="color: #cbd5e1; border: none; padding: 4px 0;">Investor DSCR originations are up <span class="teal">35%</span> annually. Self-employed investors finally have a path that uses property income, not personal W-2s.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <div class="story">
        <p>Jake, Emily, and Tom aren't exceptions. <strong>These programs exist because millions of qualified borrowers get told no when the answer should be <span class="teal">"let's look at another option"</span>.</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- === SLIDE 10: CLOSE + CONTACT === -->
<section style="background: linear-gradient(180deg, #0a0a0a 0%, #0f172a 100%);">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="slide-header">
      <div class="slide-num"></div>
      <h2 class="slide-title">The Bottom Line</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="card animate-on-scroll">
      <div class="story">
        <p>Every one of these clients had been told <span class="amber">"impossible"</span> before they walked through my door. Jake was ready to give up on homeownership. Emily was told she'd never get into Cottonwood Heights. Tom thought his deal was dead.</p>
        <p>They weren't impossible. They just needed the <span class="teal">right loan program</span>, and someone willing to look beyond the surface.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card animate-on-scroll">
      <div class="story">
        <p>VA loans. FHA flexibility. DSCR for investors. Most lenders show you one path. I find the path that <strong>actually works for your situation</strong>.</p>
        <p style="margin-top: 14px; color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.95rem;">Know someone who heard "no"? I specialize in second opinions.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="contact-box animate-on-scroll" style="margin-top: 28px;">
      <img src="qr-code.jpg" alt="Contact Tiffani" class="qr">
      <h3 style="font-size: 1.3rem; margin-bottom: 2px; color: #f8fafc;">Tiffani Swensen</h3>
      <p style="color: #64748b; font-size: 0.85rem; margin-bottom: 20px;">Real Estate Agent / Owner, Simply Home</p>
      <div style="margin: 12px 0;">
        <a href="tel:8014037779" class="btn btn-primary">Call</a>
        <a href="mailto:tiffani@simplyhome.io" class="btn btn-secondary">Email</a>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-top: 16px;">
        <p style="color: #475569; font-size: 0.8rem; margin: 3px 0;">1052 Pheasant Tail Dr, Bluffdale, UT 84065</p>
        <p style="color: #475569; font-size: 0.8rem; margin: 3px 0;">simplyhome.io</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<footer>
  <div class="container">
    <p>© 2026 Simply Home. All rights reserved. | simplyhome.io</p>
  </div>
</footer>

<script>
  const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
    entries.forEach(entry => {
      if (entry.isIntersecting) entry.target.classList.add('visible');
    });
  }, { threshold: 0.1, rootMargin: '0px 0px -30px 0px' });
  document.querySelectorAll('.animate-on-scroll').forEach(el => observer.observe(el));
</script>

</body>
</html>
